# macboot — .gitignore
#
# This repo is public. Most entries below exist to keep something specific from
# being published by accident, not to keep the tree tidy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publish: personal content
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# STRUCTURAL, not a convention to remember. 70-claude.sh creates ~/.claude/memory
# empty, and a checkout placed anywhere near it must not be able to absorb it.
# On the source machine that directory holds comp figures, employer-contract
# strategy and a private archive pointer. The bootstrap's job is to create the
# directory; publishing its contents is a one-way mistake, so the ignore rule
# ships before the first commit rather than after the first close call.
memory/

# The working design doc inventories employer repo names, unpushed-commit counts
# and absolute paths on one specific laptop. Useful to me, nobody else's business.
# README.md is therefore self-contained: it must never link into docs/specs/.
docs/specs/

# link_once() moves a pre-existing real file to <name>.bak.<timestamp> before it
# symlinks. Those backups are whatever the machine had before macboot ran —
# possibly a .zshrc with tokens in it — and they land next to the tracked files.
*.bak.*

# ensure_block() writes "$file.macboot.$$" and renames it into place. An
# interrupted run (Ctrl-C between write and mv) leaves the temp behind.
*.macboot.[0-9]*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state and test scratch the bootstrap itself writes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Belt and braces, NOT a description of where anything writes. Nothing in this repo
# executes any more, so nothing here writes anywhere at all — these patterns are left
# because a hand-made scratch dir or a stray redirect should not become a commit.
#
# The `.macboot/` entry is historical: an earlier version of this repo shipped an
# installer that kept per-module state in $MACBOOT_HOME/.macboot/state. That was in the
# HOME being set up, never in the checkout. Kept ignored so an old state directory left
# on a machine that ran it can never be committed by accident.
.macboot/
*.log
logs/
fakehome/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
